// The names in the `unguarded variable(s) …` diagnostic, against the other
// spellings of the SAME binder in the same load.
//
// `formulaToGuarded` (Theory/Constraint/System/Guarded.hs:471-479) runs the
// whole conversion inside one `Precise.evalFreshT … (avoidPrecise fmOrig)`
// (line 474), and its quantifier arms draw their binders with
// `openFormulaPrefix` (Guarded.hs:536,547) with no `scopeFreshness` around
// them — so a single supply is threaded across the entire formula.
// `noUnguardedVars` (Guarded.hs:507-514) then `show`s the survivors under
// those freshened names (line 511).  The pretty printer has its own supply:
// `prettyLNFormula` (Theory/Model/Formula.hs:518-520) seeds `avoidPrecise`
// afresh, and `prettyLFormula` opens every prefix under `scopeFreshness`
// (Theory/Model/Formula.hs:503-505), which RESTORES the supply on the way
// out.  One binder can therefore print differently in the report and in the
// echo:
//
//   - `Shadow`'s inner `x` is shadowed by the enclosing one, so both supplies
//     have consumed `x` before it is drawn: the echoed lemma reads
//     `∀ x.1 z.` and the diagnostic names 'x.1', 'z';
//   - `GuardedFirst` puts a guardable `∀ x` conjunct FIRST, where nothing
//     encloses the offending one.  The conversion carries that binder's `x`
//     across into the second conjunct and reports 'x.1', while the printer's
//     scope-restored supply prints the same conjunct `∀ x z.` — the report
//     and the echo disagree by design;
//   - `UnguardedFirst` is that formula mirrored, so the offending conjunct is
//     reached with `x` still untouched and the report reads 'x', 'z'.
//
// A supply reset per quantifier, or one counting only ENCLOSING binders,
// collapses those answers onto one.  The quoted SUBFORMULA is a spelling
// again: `noUnguardedVars` quotes it as `ppFormula f0` (Guarded.hs:513) and
// `ppFormula` (Guarded.hs:477) is `nest 2 . doubleQuotes . prettyLNFormula`,
// whose `avoidPrecise` sees that subformula alone — so it reads `"∀ x z. …"`
// beside a variable list that says 'x.1'.  `ppError` (Guarded.hs:479) prints
// the whole formula the same way, which is why the trailer under `in the
// formula` carries the printer's names and not the conversion's.
//
// Every probe here is a LEMMA on purpose.  `prettyRestriction`
// (TheoryObject.hs:889-901) decides its `// safety formula` line with
// `formulaToGuarded_` (Guarded.hs:466-467), which is `either (error . render)
// id`, so the oracle DIES while printing an unguardable restriction and the
// same formulas as restrictions yield no comparable bytes at all.  A lemma's
// conversion reaches only `checkGuarded`'s `Either`
// (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:988-993).
//
// No corpus theory carries an unguardable lemma or restriction — no corpus wf
// block holds a " Formula guardedness" header at all.
//
// Compared slices: the wf report block AND the `theory … end` echo (see
// check.sh) — the echo repeats each diagnostic inside the lemma's
// `conversion to guarded formula failed:` comment and prints the printer's
// own binder names beside it, which is half of the corner.

theory GuardedFreshenedNames
begin

lemma Shadow:
  "All x #NOW. Foo(x) @ #NOW ==> (All x z. (<x, z> = x) ==> F)"

lemma GuardedFirst:
  "(All x #i. Foo(x) @ #i ==> F) & (All x z. (<x, z> = x) ==> F)"

lemma UnguardedFirst:
  "(All x z. (<x, z> = x) ==> F) & (All x #i. Foo(x) @ #i ==> F)"

rule A:
  [ In( x ) ] --[ Foo( x ) ]-> [ ]

end
